From a6060559a28e1baa1ad45f1a4f08ccfcf77a2cdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:47:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/21] clients: latest-tracking read-only client disc +
 dvd/lite variants

fetch-clients.sh resolves each Reticulum client's latest stable GitHub release
at run time (no pinned versions), downloads a curated one-per-OS set, and
verifies against upstream checksums where published (records the rest in a
MANIFEST). The disc is built version-agnostically (build-clients-img.sh globs
dl/clients/<App>/), and build-rnsbox.sh's dvd path auto-sizes the rootfs to the
actual ISO so any "latest" fits under the image packer's ~4 GiB per-partition
limit. Client binaries are downloaded at build time and git-ignored; build-host
paths are derived from the script location. dvd = NCM + clients disc, lite =
NCM-only.
